  <h2>Research Interests</h2>
<p>
  I am interested in mathematical and statistical methodology for spatially structured biomedical data, especially
  histopathology images, single-cell omics, and related imaging-derived measurements. My current interests include
  spatial statistics, topological data analysis, graph-based methods, and computational approaches for biologically
  meaningful problems.
</p>
<p>
  I am a rising senior at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, pursuing a double major in Mathematics
  and Statistics &amp; Analytics.
</p>
